modify.\nDo NOT re-read files that are unrelated to the current step.\n\nStep 4: Build eval scorecard JSON reporter and summary test\n{\n  \"id\": \"step-4\",\n  \"title\": \"Build eval scorecard JSON reporter and summary test\",\n  \"description\": \"Create `test/golden/scorecard.ts` that exports a `generateScorecard(report: EvalReport): string` function which renders a human-readable Markdown table and a machine-readable JSON summary of all scenario results. The table should have columns: Scenario, Pass/Fail, Score%, Top Finding, Expected Pattern, Confidence, Evidence Count, Heuristic/AI. Also create `test/golden/__tests__/scorecard.test.ts` that runs all GOLDEN_EXPECTATIONS scenarios, builds the EvalReport via `buildEvalReport`, generates the scorecard, and asserts: (1) the scorecard is valid Markdown, (2) every scenario row is present, (3) overallScore > 0.9. This formalizes the eval as a regression gate.\",\n  \"requiredChecks\": [\n    \"lint\",\n    \"typecheck\",\n    \"unit\"\n  ]\n}\n\nYou are the first agent to work on this step.\nImplement the changes described above, run checks to verify, and fix any issues before handing off.\nBe thorough — the next agent will review your work and should find it correct.\n\nWhen done, explain what you reviewed, what you changed (if anything), and your assessment.\n\nEnd with:\nVerdict: approve  — if the step is complete and correct, no more changes needed\nVerdict: changes_made  — if you made fixes or improvements\nVerdict: replan_needed  — if the step is structurally impossible to complete as planned and needs controller-managed replanning"}],"timestamp":1774115977769}}
